{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VMYhTz59huhakt5TiSLibt","type":"tool_result","content":"F-03-002 | Lazy upgrade creates thread schema on arbitrary existing files\n`openThreadDatabase` unconditionally opens the supplied path and runs `runMigrations(db, buildThreadMigrations())` in `packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:85-89`. When no creation metadata is passed, v1 creates `thread_metadata` without inserting the required singleton row (`create.ts:25-44`). `messages.listMessages` then calls this opener and returns `ok: true` from `readMessages` (`packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:84-98`). A TSX probe against an existing empty file showed `messages.listMessages({ filePath })` returned `{ ok:true, value:[] }`, changed `PRAGMA user_version` from 0 to 2, and created `event`, `message`, `message_block`, and `thread_metadata` tables; a later `messageEvents` call failed with `thread file has no metadata row`. This is a newly introduced production-path regression: read-back succeeds and mutates a non-thread file instead of rejecting an invalid thread file without creating app schema.\naffected: ['packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts', 'packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts', 'packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts']","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4de8d8b1-5d3a-4643-b6ad-a0c0a326f4fa","uuid":"9a78ec73-20a7-4021-8f24-092b91a9481a","timestamp":"2026-06-10T14:11:29.976Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"F-03-002 | Lazy upgrade creates thread schema on arbitrary existing files\n`openThreadDatabase` unconditionally opens the supplied path and runs `runMigrations(db, buildThreadMigrations())` in `packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:85-89`. When no creation metadata is passed, v1 creates `thread_metadata` without inserting the required singleton row (`create.ts:25-44`). `messages.listMessages` then calls this opener and returns `ok: true` from `readMessages` (`packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts:84-98`). A TSX probe against an existing empty file showed `messages.listMessages({ filePath })` returned `{ ok:true, value:[] }`, changed `PRAGMA user_version` from 0 to 2, and created `event`, `message`, `message_block`, and `thread_metadata` tables; a later `messageEvents` call failed with `thread file has no metadata row`. This is a newly introduced production-path regression: read-back succeeds and mutates a non-thread file instead of rejecting an invalid thread file without creating app schema.\naffected: ['packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts', 'packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts', 'packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts']","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
