{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_01PhYfm2ZmeraAwJ3UvLFc2t","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All gates green. The fix is verified by the focused suite (13 tests covering both F-03-001 and F-03-002 scenarios), `green-verify` (62 tests, immutability OK), and `verify-all` (72 tests).\n\n```json\n{\n  \"outcome\": \"ready-for-verification\",\n  \"planSummary\": \"Fixed F-03-002. openThreadDatabase now performs an identity check before any migration runs: a read-only probe (so the probe itself cannot mutate an invalid file) requires schema version >= 1, a thread_metadata table, and the metadata singleton row that thread creation writes transactionally. Files failing the check — an empty database, an unrelated SQLite database, a non-database file — are rejected as caller_error/thread_not_found ('exists but is not an lhc thread file') with no lhc tables created and user_version untouched; SQLite's 'not a database' refusal is classified as the same identity failure, while other open errors remain system_error. The opener's signature changed to OpResult<DatabaseSync> so the rejection flows through the standard result contract, and all three call sites (runMessageEvents, runListEvents, listMessages) propagate it. Valid Story 2 user_version=1 files pass the check (they carry the metadata row) and still migrate lazily to v2, so F-03-001 behavior is preserved — all prior migration tests stay green. Three focused tests prove rejection-without-mutation for an existing empty file (verifier's exact probe), an unrelated SQLite database with foreign data, and a plain text file.\",\n  \"changedFiles\": [\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts\", \"reason\": \"Added validateThreadFile (read-only identity probe: version >= 1, thread_metadata table, singleton row) run before migrations; openThreadDatabase now returns OpResult<DatabaseSync>, rejecting non-thread files as caller_error/thread_not_found and wrapping environment failures as system_error\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts\", \"reason\": \"runMessageEvents and runListEvents consume the opener's OpResult, returning the rejection instead of opening/migrating arbitrary files\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts\", \"reason\": \"listMessages consumes the opener's OpResult, so read-back on a non-thread file fails instead of adopting the file\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/thread-migration.test.ts\", \"reason\": \"Added an F-03-002 describe block: three rejection tests asserting error class/code and, below the SDK, unchanged user_version, no lhc tables created, foreign data and raw bytes intact; F-03-001 tests unchanged above it\" },\n    { \"path\": \"packages/lhc/test/red-manifest.json\", \"reason\": \"Re-recorded thread-migration.test.ts hash after appending the F-03-002 tests\" }\n  ],\n  \"tests\": {\n    \"added\": [\n      \"test/thread-migration.test.ts: listMessages against an existing empty database file fails with caller_error/thread_not_found, user_version stays 0, no tables created (the verifier's exact F-03-002 probe)\",\n      \"test/thread-migration.test.ts: messageEvents against an unrelated SQLite database fails, creates no lhc tables, leaves user_version at 0 and the foreign rows intact\",\n      \"test/thread-migration.test.ts: a non-SQLite text file is rejected as caller_error/thread_not_found by both listMessages and messageEvents with its bytes byte-identical afterward\"\n    ],\n    \"modified\": [],\n    \"removed\": [],\n    \"totalAfterStory\": 72,\n    \"deltaFromPriorBaseline\": 14\n  },\n  \"gatesRun\": [\n    { \"command\": \"npx vitest run test/thread-migration.test.ts test/projection.test.ts\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --dir packages/lhc run green-verify\", \"result\": \"pass\" },\n    { \"command\": \"pnpm --dir packages/lhc run verify-all\", \"result\": \"pass\" }\n  ],\n  \"selfReview\": {\n    \"findingsFixed\": [\n      \"F-03-002: the lazy opener no longer creates lhc schema on, or returns successful read-back from, arbitrary existing files — a read-only identity probe (schema version >= 1 plus the thread_metadata singleton) gates migration, invalid existing files are rejected as caller_error/thread_not_found without any mutation, and Story 2 user_version=1 files still migrate lazily (all F-03-001 tests remain green)\"\n    ],\n    \"findingsSurfaced\": [\n      \"The 'not a database' classification relies on SQLite's error message text to distinguish identity failures from environment failures; node:sqlite exposes no stable error code for SQLITE_NOTADB, so a wording change in a future Node release would downgrade that case to system_error (still a rejection, never adoption) — worth a glance when bumping the Node engine\",\n      \"thread_not_found is reused for 'exists but is not a thread file' because the epic's error-code set is closed; the reason string distinguishes the cases. If operators need to tell them apart programmatically, a dedicated code would be a vocabulary addition for a future story\",\n      \"The read-only probe adds one extra open per SDK operation on a thread file; negligible at v1 scale, and it is the only way to guarantee the probe itself cannot mutate an invalid file\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"openQuestions\": [],\n  \"specDeviations\": [],\n  \"recommendedNextStep\": \"Re-verify F-03-002 with the new rejection tests (the original empty-file probe now returns caller_error/thread_not_found with user_version still 0 and no tables); F-03-001 coverage is unchanged and green. Then proceed to Story 4, whose turn tables should land as a version-3 migration behind the same validated opener.\"\n}\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":532,"cache_read_input_tokens":170878,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":532},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4de8d8b1-5d3a-4643-b6ad-a0c0a326f4fa","uuid":"0348f0fd-5fbf-408e-905a-71acd28fec80","request_id":"req_011CbuihqcJQK4LxGZ8wHmwK"}
